[{"answer":"Hello everyone.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/1.mp3"},{"answer":"Today we're going to look at another natural food product","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/2.mp3"},{"answer":"and that's maple syrup.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/3.mp3"},{"answer":"What is this exactly?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/4.mp3"},{"answer":"Well, maple syrup looks rather like clear honey,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/5.mp3"},{"answer":"but it's not made by bees;","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/6.mp3"},{"answer":"it's produced from the plant fluid, or sap, inside the maple tree","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/7.mp3"},{"answer":"and that makes maple syrup a very natural product.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/8.mp3"},{"answer":"Maple syrup is a thick, golden, sweet-tasting liquid","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/9.mp3"},{"answer":"that can be bought in bottles or jars","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/10.mp3"},{"answer":"and poured onto food such as waffles and ice cream","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/11.mp3"},{"answer":"or used in the baking of cakes and pastries.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/12.mp3"},{"answer":"It contains no preservatives or added ingredients,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/13.mp3"},{"answer":"and it provides a healthy alternative to refined sugar.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/14.mp3"},{"answer":"Let's just talk a bit about the maple tree itself,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/15.mp3"},{"answer":"which is where maple syrup comes from.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/16.mp3"},{"answer":"So, there are many species of maple tree,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/17.mp3"},{"answer":"and they'll grow without fertilizer in areas where there's plenty of moisture in the soil.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/18.mp3"},{"answer":"However, they'll only do this if another important criterion is fulfilled,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/19.mp3"},{"answer":"which is that they must have full or partial sun exposure during the day and very cool nights,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/20.mp3"},{"answer":"and I'll talk more about that in a minute.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/21.mp3"},{"answer":"There are only certain parts of the world that provide all these conditions:","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/22.mp3"},{"answer":"one is Canada,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/23.mp3"},{"answer":"and by that, I mean all parts of Canada,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/24.mp3"},{"answer":"and the other is the north-eastern states of North America.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/25.mp3"},{"answer":"In these areas, the climate suits the trees perfectly.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/26.mp3"},{"answer":"In fact, Canada produces over two-thirds of the world's maple syrup,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/27.mp3"},{"answer":"which is why the five-pointed maple leaf is a Canadian symbol","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/28.mp3"},{"answer":"and has featured on the flag since 1964.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/29.mp3"},{"answer":"So how did maple syrup production begin?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/30.mp3"},{"answer":"Well, long before Europeans settled in these parts of the world,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/31.mp3"},{"answer":"the indigenous communities had started producing maple sugar.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/32.mp3"},{"answer":"They bored holes in the trunks of maple trees","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/33.mp3"},{"answer":"and used containers made of tree bark to collect the liquid sap as it poured out.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/34.mp3"},{"answer":"As they were unable to keep the liquid for any length of time,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/35.mp3"},{"answer":"they didn't have storage facilities in those days,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/36.mp3"},{"answer":"they boiled the liquid by placing pieces of rock that had become scorching hot from the sun into the sap.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/37.mp3"},{"answer":"They did this until it turned into sugar,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/38.mp3"},{"answer":"and they were then able to use this to sweeten their food and drinks.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/39.mp3"},{"answer":"Since that time, improvements have been made to the process,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/40.mp3"},{"answer":"but it has changed very little overall.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/41.mp3"},{"answer":"So let's look at the production of maple syrup today.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/42.mp3"},{"answer":"Clearly, the maple forests are a valuable resource in many Canadian and North American communities.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/43.mp3"},{"answer":"The trees have to be well looked after","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/44.mp3"},{"answer":"and they cannot be used to make syrup until the trunks reach a diameter of around 25 centimetres.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/45.mp3"},{"answer":"This can take anything up to 40 years.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/46.mp3"},{"answer":"As I've already mentioned,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/47.mp3"},{"answer":"maple trees need the right conditions to grow and also to produce sap.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/48.mp3"},{"answer":"Why is this?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/49.mp3"},{"answer":"Well, what happens is that during a cold night,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/50.mp3"},{"answer":"the tree absorbs water from the soil,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/51.mp3"},{"answer":"and that rises through the tree's vascular system.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/52.mp3"},{"answer":"But then in the warmer daytime,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/53.mp3"},{"answer":"the change in temperature causes the water to be pushed back down to the bottom of the tree.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/54.mp3"},{"answer":"This continual movement, up and down,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/55.mp3"},{"answer":"leads to the formation of the sap needed for maple syrup production.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/56.mp3"},{"answer":"When the tree is ready,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/57.mp3"},{"answer":"it can be tapped and this involves drilling a small hole into the trunk","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/58.mp3"},{"answer":"and inserting a tube into it that ends in a bucket.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/59.mp3"},{"answer":"The trees can often take several taps,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/60.mp3"},{"answer":"though the workers take care not to cause any damage to the healthy growth of the tree itself.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/61.mp3"},{"answer":"The sap that comes out of the trees consists of 98% water","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/62.mp3"},{"answer":"and 2% sugar and other nutrients.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/63.mp3"},{"answer":"It has to be boiled so that much of that water evaporates,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/64.mp3"},{"answer":"and this process has to take place immediately, using what are called evaporators.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/65.mp3"},{"answer":"These are basically extremely large pans,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/66.mp3"},{"answer":"the sap is poured into these,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/67.mp3"},{"answer":"a fire is built and the pans are then heated until the sap boils.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/68.mp3"},{"answer":"As it does this, the water evaporates, and the syrup begins to form.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/69.mp3"},{"answer":"The evaporation process creates large quantities of steam,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/70.mp3"},{"answer":"and the sap becomes thicker and denser, and, at just the right moment,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/71.mp3"},{"answer":"when the sap is thick enough to be called maple syrup,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/72.mp3"},{"answer":"the worker removes it from the heat.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/73.mp3"},{"answer":"After this process, something called 'sugar sand' has to be filtered out","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/74.mp3"},{"answer":"as this builds up during the boiling and gives the syrup a cloudy appearance and a slightly gritty taste.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/75.mp3"},{"answer":"Once this has been done,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/76.mp3"},{"answer":"the syrup is ready to be packaged so that it can be used for a whole variety of products.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/77.mp3"},{"answer":"It takes 40 litres of sap to produce one litre of maple syrup","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/78.mp3"},{"answer":"so you can get an idea of how much is needed!","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/79.mp3"},{"answer":"So that's the basic process...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-17-test-4-section-4-2022-12-27-23-54-16/80.mp3"}]
